<Layout title="About" description="How the BUSY Bar app library mirrors complete apps, credits their authors, and supports community ideas."><article class="prose-page"><span class="eyebrow">The Public Workbench</span><h1>About This Library</h1><p>BUSY Bar Apps is Ted Tschopp’s library of apps and ideas for the BUSY Bar. It brings the searchable catalog and reading experience of <a href="https://ai.tedt.org/">AI.Tedt.org</a> to a small display with many possible jobs.</p><h2>Complete Apps, Traceable Sources</h2><p>The community catalog mirrors <a href="https://github.com/maxswinkels/busybar-apps">Max Swinkels’s BUSY Bar Apps repository</a>. Each app keeps its original author, source files, supporting assets, and license notices. Downloads include the full app folder, with hashes and an upstream commit on the detail page.</p><p>The importer checks for additions and updates daily at 3 a.m. Pacific. Publication follows validation and a successful build. GitHub’s scheduler can run later than the requested time. See <a href={`${repo}/actions`}>the update history</a> for actual runs.</p><p>Apps that disappear upstream are marked archived. Their last mirrored version remains available. Direct community submissions are stored separately and reviewed through pull requests.</p><h2>Ideas and Conversations</h2><p>Ratings, comments, and app ideas live in <a href={`${repo}/discussions`}>this repository’s GitHub Discussions</a>. These are this site’s community records. Ratings from other galleries are not copied into the score.</p><h2>What the Download Number Means</h2><p>A download start is an action on an app’s complete-package download button on this website. It does not prove that the transfer finished or that the app was installed. Copies of source code and individual-file downloads are excluded.</p><p>The counter stores app totals and random event IDs used to prevent duplicate retries. It does not store IP addresses, accounts, or browsing histories. Counting is best effort; a counter outage never prevents a download.</p><h2 id="attribution">Credits and Licenses</h2><p>Catalog apps and previews are contributed under MIT by their respective authors. Their notices are retained in the mirrored files and complete packages. Gallery source is MIT. See the <a href={`${repo}/blob/main/LICENSE`}>license</a> and <a href={`${repo}/blob/main/docs/UPSTREAM-LICENSE`}>upstream notice</a>.</p><p>BUSY brand and device artwork is © Flipper Devices under CC BY 4.0. Inter, Cal Sans, Fira Code, and Titillium Web are used under their respective open font licenses. The site design follows TedT.org’s Public Workbench system.</p><p>This is an unofficial community site, unaffiliated with and not endorsed or supported by Flipper Devices. “BUSY Bar” is their trademark.</p></article></Layout>
